        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "5638f919-f246-5a99-a5a3-ab14a6cf1ae6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charles White Whittlesey, Ernst von Hoeppner\n- Organizations: United States Army, German Air Service, 82nd Division\n- Military units: 326th Infantry Regiment, Lost Battalion\n- Events: World War I, Meuse-Argonne Offensive, final Allied offensive on the Western Front\n- Roles: Lieutenant Colonel, Commanding General, Prussian cavalry officer, Medal of Honor recipient\n\nFacts:\n- Ernst von Hoeppner was a Prussian cavalry officer who served as Commanding General of the German Air Service during World War I.\n- The Meuse-Argonne Offensive was a major part of the final Allied offensive of World War I and stretched along the entire Western Front.\n- The 326th Infantry Regiment was a United States Army infantry regiment in the 82nd Division that saw active service during World War I and fought in the Meuse-Argonne Offensive.\n- In October 1918, Charles White Whittlesey led the Lost Battalion in the Meuse-Argonne Offensive during the final stages of World War I.\n- Charles White Whittlesey was a United States Army lieutenant colonel and an American Medal of Honor recipient.\n- The 326th Infantry Regiment was inactivated in 1919.\n- Charles White Whittlesey was presumed dead on November 26, 1921.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "81360362-0620-5b83-becd-e5bdeb7fe27d",
        "text": "Page: Charles White Whittlesey. Sentence: Lieutenant Colonel Charles White Whittlesey (January 20, 1884 – presumed dead November 26, 1921) was a United States Army officer and an American Medal of Honor recipient who led the \"Lost Battalion\" in the Meuse-Argonne Offensive in October 1918 during the final stages of World War I.\nPage: Meuse-Argonne Offensive. Sentence: The Meuse-Argonne Offensive, also known as the Maas-Argonne Offensive and the Battle of the Argonne Forest, was a major part of the final Allied offensive of World War I that stretched along the entire Western Front.\nPage: 326th Infantry Regiment (United States). Sentence: The 326th Infantry Regiment was an infantry regiment of the United States Army that saw active service during World War I, as part of the 82nd Division and fought in the Meuse-Argonne Offensive and was inactivated in 1919.\nPage: Ernst von Hoeppner. Sentence: Ernst Wilhelm Arnold von Hoeppner (14 January 1860 – 26 September 1922) was a Prussian cavalry officer who served as the Commanding General of the German Air Service (\"Luftstreitkräfte\") during World War I.",
